  "notes": [
   "Times are medians of repeated calls with a device synchronization around each; values rounded to 5 significant digits.",
   "Kymatio medians come from an earlier run of the same script on the same pod and GPU (its timing does not depend on the curvelets code); only medians were logged, so min_ms is null.",
   "Kymatio is not invertible and was not run at 2048x2048: building its filter bank on the CPU took over 20 minutes.",
   "Kymatio and dtcwt do not provide 3D rows here (Kymatio's 3D scattering is a different transform; dtcwt 3D is included).",
   "The dtcwt OpenCL and TensorFlow rows were measured in a later pod session of the same GPU model (RTX 3070, driver 580.95.05), with TensorFlow 2.21.0 and PyOpenCL 2026.1.5. The OpenCL driver had to be registered in the container (/etc/OpenCL/vendors/nvidia.icd).",
   "dtcwt OpenCL rows pass NumPy arrays in and out, so they include the host/device copies. The dtcwt TensorFlow backend is written for TensorFlow 1; it was run in graph mode through tf.compat.v1 aliases, with the outputs fetched to the host. Both backends were checked against the NumPy backend (coefficients agree to 1e-3 of their scale) before being timed.",
   "dtcwt OpenCL 3D was not timed: its highpass coefficients differ from the NumPy backend's (the lowpass agrees)."
  ]
 },
